1284+ 6509              ; ------------------------------------------------------------
1285+ 6509              ; FTP upload CPU speed limit
1286+ 6509              ;
1287+ 6509              ; ESP8266/ESP-AT upload was tested at 3456000 baud:
1288+ 6509              ;
1289+ 6509              ;   3.5 MHz  - OK
1290+ 6509              ;   7 MHz    - OK
1291+ 6509              ;   14 MHz   - FAIL
1292+ 6509              ;   20 MHz   - FAIL
1293+ 6509              ;
1294+ 6509              ; Failure at 14/20 MHz is not caused by CIPSEND packet size.
1295+ 6509              ; Even 256-byte packets may fail at 20 MHz.
1296+ 6509              ;
1297+ 6509              ; AT+CIPSEND handshake itself is OK at 20 MHz - ESP returns
1298+ 6509              ; the '>' prompt correctly. send_data also reports successful
1299+ 6509              ; transmission, but ESP responses show timing-dependent states
1300+ 6509              ; such as:
1301+ 6509              ;
1302+ 6509              ;   busy s...
1303+ 6509              ;   Recv <n> bytes
1304+ 6509              ;   busy s...
1305+ 6509              ;   SEND OK
1306+ 6509              ;
1307+ 6509              ; At high CPU speed ESP may not reliably complete reception of
1308+ 6509              ; the serial data stream although the local UART reports ready.
1309+ 6509              ;
1310+ 6509              ; Therefore FTP upload is intentionally limited to 7 MHz.
1311+ 6509              ; Download works reliably at 20 MHz.
1312+ 6509              ;
1313+ 6509              ; Tested with 2048-byte CIPSEND packets.
1314+ 6509              ; ------------------------------------------------------------
1315+ 6509
1316+ 6509
1317+ 6509
